Write a `.rust-mutants.toml` whose every value is already the default

Usage: rust-mutants init [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --color <WHEN>
          Whether to paint the output. `auto` paints a terminal that has not set `NO_COLOR`

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Colour a terminal that has not asked to go without
          - always: Always
          - never:  Never
          
          [default: auto]

      --root <DIR>
          The workspace root. Defaults to the working directory

      --cargo <PATH>
          Run this cargo, by path, rather than the one found on the `PATH`; its rustc is the one
          beside it

      --force
          Overwrite a file that is already there

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
